        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add readiness conditions and providers",
        "body": "Related RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/33\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nOpenClaw already exposes Gateway `/ready` and `/readyz`, but readiness is evaluated by a fixed set of Gateway checks. Hosts and operators cannot select the additional criteria that define readiness for a deployment, plugins cannot contribute bounded observational evidence, and CLI, health, and status surfaces do not share one canonical result.\r\n\r\nThat leaves Docker, Kubernetes, systemd, OCC, and other hosts maintaining private scripts to answer a basic question: is this OpenClaw instance ready to accept work under its configured requirements?\r\n\r\n## Proposal\r\n\r\nThis draft implements the readiness portion of RFC 0018:\r\n\r\n- normalize Gateway startup, admission, drain, selected-channel, suppressed-channel, event-loop, and workspace evidence into structured conditions\r\n- distinguish required conditions, which fail readiness on `False` or `Unknown`, from advisory conditions, which remain visible without changing the ready result\r\n- let operators select built-in and plugin-contributed criteria directly with `gateway.readiness`\r\n- let activated plugins register namespaced, self-describing criteria through the public plugin registry\r\n- bound plugin checks with per-criterion timeouts, an overall readiness deadline, stable timeout/error results, short caching, and in-flight coalescing\r\n- project the same canonical result through `/ready`, `/readyz`, Gateway `ready`, health, status, and `openclaw ready`\r\n- provide human-readable and `--json` CLI output with fail-closed exit status\r\n\r\nExample operator selection:\r\n\r\n```json5\r\n{\r\n  gateway: {\r\n    readiness: {\r\n      requiredCriteria: [\"openclaw.workspace-writable\", \"plugin.example.dependency\"],\r\n      advisoryCriteria: [\"plugin.metrics.exporter\"],\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nA plugin may contribute observational evidence without changing readiness by default:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\napi.registerReadinessCriterion({\r\n  id: \"dependency\",\r\n  description: \"Example dependency is reachable\",\r\n  async check({ pluginConfig, signal }) {\r\n    const reachable = await probeDependency(pluginConfig, { signal });\r\n    return reachable\r\n      ? { status: \"True\", reason: \"DependencyReachable\" }\r\n      : { status: \"False\", reason: \"DependencyUnavailable\" };\r\n  },\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\nCore publishes that registration as `plugin.<plugin-id>.dependency`. Operators explicitly select it as `requiredCriteria` when it belongs in their serving contract.\r\n\r\n## Compatibility\r\n\r\nExisting `/ready` and `/readyz` routes remain available and retain their HTTP contract: `200` when all required conditions are true and `503` otherwise. Existing installations need no readiness configuration; the Gateway lifecycle baseline always applies, while explicitly selected criteria add richer deployment-specific evidence.\r\n\r\nThis PR does **not** add hosting profiles, profile selection, node-mode profiles, runtime activation identity, release conformance, Lobster concepts, tenant concepts, OCC resources, or policy/doctor dependencies. Standard Hosting Profiles are intentionally separated into RFC 0023 so this readiness facility can stand on its own.\r\n\r\n## Review Stack\r\n\r\nThis is one upstream PR with four commits. The fork PRs preserve the same smaller review boundaries:\r\n\r\n- [PR 17: canonical Gateway readiness conditions](https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/17)\r\n- [PR 22: workspace writability criterion](https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/22)\r\n- [PR 23: selectable readiness providers](https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/23)\r\n- [PR 27: canonical `openclaw ready` CLI](https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/27)\r\n\r\nThe branch is rebased onto current `openclaw/main`; the plugin registration slice is adapted to the current modular registry.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- focused readiness, Gateway, status, and CLI suites pass\r\n- exact-head readiness/config/status/CLI shard: 64 assertions passed\r\n- formatting and `git diff --check` pass\r\n- plugin SDK export count matches the updated expected surface\r\n- Codex review findings fixed: the CLI now calls the canonical Gateway evaluator, and live readiness is projected through both health and status RPCs\r\n- ClawSweeper findings fixed: workspace probing is observational and canonical config help/label metadata covers gateway.readiness\r\n\r\nFull local typecheck is not claimed: the shared dependency tree has unrelated baseline errors, and this machine runs Node 24.14 while current OpenClaw requires Node 24.15+ for the embedded SQLite safety floor. Exact-head packaged Docker proof remains follow-up evidence for this draft.\r\n",
        "branch": "user/giodl/readiness-profiles-upstream",
